course: dictionary
lesson: 6929
title: Padding: soft filling, extra words, and screen space
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Padding is a noun, and it has three main meanings. The first is soft material that fills or covers something to make it comfortable or to protect it. «The shin bone, the tibia, lies just under the skin with little padding, which is why kicks hurt.» Here, padding is the soft layer that protects, and little padding means less protection.
explain: The second meaning is extra words or material added to make something longer but not better. Your teacher may say, «avoid padding: write what matters.» Padding in this sense is words that take up space but do not help the reader.
explain: The third meaning is used in computing. On a web page, padding is the space inside a box, between the words and the edge of the box. Check which meaning fits by looking at the words around it: soft filling, extra words, or empty space on a screen.
fact: Padding means soft material used to fill or cover something, to make it comfortable or to protect it.
fact: Padding can also mean extra words added to make something longer but not better.
fact: On a computer screen or web page, padding is the space inside a box.
fact: Helmets, shin guards and car seats use padding to absorb the force of a bump.
fact: Good check: swap in «filling» or «cushioning» for the soft meaning, or «extra words» for the writing meaning, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The shin bone lies just under the skin with little padding, which is why kicks hurt.» What does padding mean here? | Space inside a web page box | *Soft covering that protects | A type of shoe | Extra words added to a story
exercise: Your teacher says, «avoid padding: write what matters.» What does padding mean here? | Space around a picture on a screen | Protective gear for football | *Extra words that make writing longer but not better | Soft material in a cushion
exercise: On a web page, what does padding mean? | *The space inside a box | A hard shell on a helmet | Thick soft material for a sofa | Extra words in an essay
test: Why do footballers wear shin guards, and what does padding do in them? | Padding makes them look smart, so they can be seen by the referee | Padding stops the ball from going in the goal | Padding makes the guards heavy so they stay in place | *Padding absorbs the force of a kick, so the leg is protected
test: Sam writes a long essay full of extra words that add nothing. Which word from the lesson describes his extra words? | *Padding | Helmet | Tibia | Fibula
exam: Which sentence uses padding to mean extra words? | The web page had padding around each box. | The car seat had padding to absorb a bump. | *Her essay was full of padding that said the same thing three times. | The cushion had thick padding to keep it soft.
